      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both the `RunFlashFw` and `RunFlashCmd` subroutines duplicate the exact same code block to trigger a system reset upon successful completion before returning `0`. Lifting this logic to `main()` centralizes the success-path behavior and cleanly separates flash logic from teardown logic.\n\n### Detailed Fix\n\n**Location:** `util/egis/et171_flash.cc`\n\nDelete the `brom.SystemReset()` blocks from the bottom of `RunFlashFw` and `RunFlashCmd`. Then, implement it conditionally at the end of `main()`.\n\n```c\n  // 4. Dispatch to chosen mode\n  int status \u003d -1;\n  if (config.mode \u003d\u003d \"flashfw\") {\n    status \u003d RunFlashFw(config, brom);\n  } else if (config.mode \u003d\u003d \"flashcmd\") {\n    status \u003d RunFlashCmd(config, boot_comm, brom);\n  } else {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Unknown or unhandled mode: {}\", config.mode);\n  }\n\n  // Execute system reset centrally on success\n  if (status \u003d\u003d 0) {\n    if (auto res \u003d brom.SystemReset(); !res) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"[WARN] System reset command failed: {}\", ToString(res.error()));\n    }\n  }\n\n  return status;\n}\n\n```",
